{
  "dom_id": "step-q87780",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Write $\\frac{12{x}^{3}}{4{x}^{2}+5}$ in the form $ax+\\frac{bx}{4{x}^{2}+5},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator to put $4{x}^{2}$ in parentheses. Then, we add and subtract $5$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12{x}^{3}}{4{x}^{2}+5} & =\\frac{3x(4{x}^{2})}{4{x}^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x(4{x}^{2}+5-5)}{4{x}^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x(4{x}^{2}+5)+3x(-5)}{4{x}^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x(4{x}^{2}+5)-15x}{4{x}^{2}+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x(4{x}^{2}+5)-15x}{4{x}^{2}+5} & =\\frac{3x(4{x}^{2}+5)}{4{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{-15x}{4{x}^{2}+5} \\\\  & =3x+\\frac{-15x}{4{x}^{2}+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=3$ and $b=-15,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=3+(-15)=-12.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
